{
    "_": [
        "Control offsets for the Fireface UCX II, and the rules that turn",
        "one into a register address. Extracted from upstream's",
        "device_ffucxii.c at the pinned revision, then checked on the wire:",
        "docs/register-addresses.md lists the eleven addresses measured and",
        "which rule each one exercises.",
        "",
        "The numbers are Michael Forney's, under ISC, the same as the code",
        "quoted under patches/. They live here because a table extracted",
        "from upstream on demand is not independent of upstream, which was",
        "the whole point of writing them down.",
        "",
        "Re-extracted at f2fdd5e: the only arithmetic that changed is Room",
        "EQ, whose ctltoreg now writes to a 0x3400 base while regtoctl keeps",
        "reading the 0x35D0 block -- a split range, measured on the wire on",
        "outputs 1 (0x3403) and 5 (0x3483)."
    ],
    "source": "michaelforney/oscmix device_ffucxii.c",
    "revision": "f2fdd5ec78338848754aad32cc07f3440de63395",
    "extracted": "2026-08-28",
    "rules": {
        "channel": "idx << 6 | offset, idx = input index or 20 + output index",
        "mix": "0x2000 | out << 6 | in            (pan)",
        "mixlevel": "0x4000 | out << 6 | idx       (level; idx = input, or 20 + playback)",
        "roomeq": "offset + (out << 5), offsets carry the 0x35D0 base the device REPORTS from",
        "roomeq-write": "the roomeq address minus 0x1D0: since f2fdd5e, writes land at the 0x3400 base while reports stay at 0x35D0 (upstream #33)"
    },
